=== DynamoDB Local method and cleanup ===
Owned container: platform-agent-p5d-dynamodb, amazon/dynamodb-local:latest,
127.0.0.1:8105 -> 8000, -inMemory -sharedDb, --rm.
Python boto3 created p5d-users(username HASH) and p5d-audit(audit_id HASH).
Next used DASHBOARD_DATA_SOURCE=aws, AWS_ROLE_ARN empty,
AWS_ENDPOINT_URL and AWS_ENDPOINT_URL_DYNAMODB=http://127.0.0.1:8105,
dummy AWS credentials, DASHBOARD_USERS_TABLE=p5d-users, DASHBOARD_AUDIT_TABLE=p5d-audit.
Auth.js local-dev session was admin. Before each role edit the fixture write grant
was updated independently; actual consistent GetItem after the users POST proved
its current value and read tenants remained. Audit table had two actual records.
Removing the users table made the users POST return 500 (no demo success).
Container stopped and --rm removed it; docker ps -a filter returned no match.
All owned Next processes terminated; lsof port 3105 returned no listener.

